KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26
^file main\.cpp line \d+: static assertion failed: f\(\) is 4$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
static_assert condition could not be evaluated
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The program is ill-formed: GCC 16 reports "static assertion failed: f() is
4".  CBMC's constant evaluator did not evaluate throw and try
(cpp26_constexpr_exception), and a static_assert whose condition it cannot
evaluate is skipped with the warning "static_assert condition could not be
evaluated; the assertion is not checked", so verification succeeded.  The
static_assert is the check that must fail, so there is no WRONG assertion.
